      body: "An implant replaces the root with a titanium post in the bone, then a crown on top. It does not touch the neighbouring teeth, and it keeps the bone under the gap in use. It needs enough bone and healthy gums, and takes about three to six months from start to finish.\n\nA bridge uses the teeth on either side as supports. It is quicker, often two or three weeks, but those teeth are trimmed for crowns. It suits a gap whose neighbours already need crowns.\n\nA removable denture costs the least and needs no surgery. It can feel bulky, and it has to come out for cleaning.\n\nThe cost on the day is only part of the comparison. Ask how long each option usually lasts, what care it needs, and what it would cost to redo. The final choice and cost depend on your examination and scan.",
